@startuml SplitSmartConsolidatedDeployment
title SplitSmart Consolidated Cloud Deployment
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

node "User devices" as devices {
  artifact "Web browser" as browser
  artifact "Android app" as android
  artifact "iOS app" as ios
}
cloud "Cloud environment" as cloud {
  node "Public edge" as edge {
    component "CDN / WAF" as waf
    component "API gateway" as gateway
  }
  node "Application tier" as app {
    component "Java 21 Spring Boot instances" as backend
    component "Notification worker" as worker
  }
  database "Managed PostgreSQL" as postgres
  queue "Durable queue" as queue
  folder "Private receipt object storage" as receipts
  component "Central logs, metrics, traces" as observability
  component "Managed secrets" as secrets
  database "Encrypted backup/PITR storage" as backup
  component "Recovery and restore process" as recovery
}
cloud "External services" as external {
  component "Email provider" as email
}

browser --> waf : HTTPS
android --> waf : HTTPS
ios --> waf : HTTPS
waf --> gateway
gateway --> backend : HTTPS/internal TLS
backend --> postgres : TLS
backend --> receipts : signed object access
backend --> queue
queue --> worker
worker --> postgres
backend --> observability
worker --> observability
backend --> email
backend --> secrets : runtime secrets
worker --> secrets : runtime secrets
postgres --> backup : encrypted backup/PITR stream
receipts --> backup : object/version backup
backup --> recovery : restore source
recovery --> postgres : restore/verify
recovery --> receipts : restore/verify

note bottom of cloud
Backend instances are stateless and scale horizontally.
PostgreSQL transactions are the consistency boundary.
Recovery targets are operational decisions; no unapproved RPO/RTO is shown.
end note
@enduml
